##
## modelstack_framework — NOT PART OF THIS PRODUCT (operator decision, 2026-09-14)
##
# This project is a browser extension. The self-maintenance harness it was scaffolded with
# (`modelstack init`), the vendored runtime unit it pins, and the gates/tests that exist only to
# police that harness are all supplied by the FRAMEWORK — they are not shipped to users and they are
# not this project's code. Nothing in this section belongs in the extension's history.
#
# The whole tree stays on disk: `modelstack sync`/`drift_check` still work (they read the worktree,
# not the index), and AGENTS.md still documents the harness. What changes is only what git carries.
#
# Consequence, stated rather than assumed: AGENTS.md's earlier rule — "commit `vendor/` beside
# `modelstack.lock` in the same commit" — no longer holds. The pin is now provenance that lives in
# the worktree; a rollback re-materialises the unit with `modelstack sync --target . --from
# <unit_revision>` (that is what `unit_revision` is for — it needs no git history).

# The vendored unit + its content-addressed pin
/vendor/
/modelstack.lock

# The scaffold's own files: rules/playbooks, the registry, the config fragments, the guards
/AGENTS.md
/.gitattributes
/.env.fragment
/PROJECTS.fragment.json
/ISSUE_template.md
/config.yaml
/registry.yaml
/pipeline.yaml
/lanes.yaml
/stack_adapter.py
/housekeeping_guard.py
/???.fragment
/*.fragment
/reasonix.toml*
/.reasonix/
/reasonix.exe
/reasonix.exe.prev-*
/reasonix

# Framework-only gates/tests: they validate the harness above, not the extension
/scripts/input_budget_report.py
/scripts/verify_lanes.py
/scripts/muse_gate.py
/test/unit/housekeeping_guard.test.js
/test/unit/lanes_aliases.test.js
/test/unit/input_budget_alignment.test.js

# Working state — scratch, telemetry, run logs, archived handoffs. None of it is product, and the
# load-bearing parts (the issue archive the housekeeping guard reads) are regenerated by the guard,
# not restored from git.
/temp/

# Browser-gate and probe screenshots (generated output from scripts/screenshot.js and the collage
# probes). They are run artifacts, not evidence — the measurements they fed live in docs/.
/shots/

##
## Reviewer / consultation artifacts — NOT PART OF THE PRODUCT (operator decision, 2026-09-14)
##
# Muse and the visual-gate reviewers produce a file per round: the brief sent, the raw reply, and a
# verdict. They are the *process*, not the product — a reader of this repository needs the
# measurement a round produced, which lives in the track's `final_report.md`, the README, and the
# committed frames, not the transcript of asking for it.
#
# Measured at the time of this rule: 252 such files were tracked (136 under docs/, 116 under
# conductor/archive/). They stay on disk — the harness still writes and reads them — they are simply
# not carried in this project's history.
#
# Patterns are the artifact SHAPES, not a directory, so a future track cannot re-add them by naming
# its evidence directory something slightly different.
**/reviews-phase*/
**/reviews/
**/consult/
**/consult-*.md
**/consult_*.md
**/consult_log.md
**/muse_review*.md
**/vision_review*.md
**/*_execution_review*.md

# A study of the FLEET's relay routing, produced by the self-maintenance harness. It is not a
# property of this extension, so it is not this project's history either.
/docs/relay-routing-conversion-20260913/

##
## Process documentation — NOT SHIPPED, NOT TRACKED (operator decision, 2026-09-14)
##
# `conductor/` is the track-management apparatus (specs, plans, gate records, close-out reports) and
# `docs/` is the per-track evidence it points at (measurements, captures, audit reports). Both are
# how the work was RUN, not what the extension IS: the shipped artefact is the MV3 extension built
# from `js/`, `assets/`, `manifest.json` — none of which lives here.
#
# Measured at the time of this rule: 780 files (404 under docs/, 376 under conductor/) — 65% of
# everything tracked. They stay on disk; the specs, plans and capture harnesses still read and write
# them (44 tracked files under test/, scripts/ and js/ reference these paths, and they keep working
# because the tree is untouched). What changes is only what git carries.
#
# Release history is NOT lost: README.md and CHANGELOG.md stay tracked at the root and are the
# human-readable record of every version this chain ships.
/conductor/
/docs/
